# Vendor Pay - Payment Approval Workflow Project

>>Prerequisites

PHP = 8.2
Composer
Node.js & npm
MySQL database  
Git


>>Installation Steps

1. Clone or setup the project repository.
2. Install PHP dependencies
	composer install
	npm install
3. Set up a new Laravel project using Composer (no extra external packages are used): 
	composer create-project laravel/laravel vendor_pay
	cd vendor_pay
4. Set configuration: cp .env.example .env



>>Database Setup

1. Open .env file and configure database connection settings:

DB_CONNECTION=mysql
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_PORT=3306
DB_DATABASE=payment_workflow
DB_USERNAME=root
DB_PASSWORD=

2. Create an empty database named payment_workflow in MySQL 

3. Generate Application Key: php artisan key:generate

>>Migration and Seeding Procedure

1. Run the database migrations and seed the pre-defined roles, vendors, users, and rule configurations:  
	php artisan migrate:fresh --seed



>>Login Credentials

Username of Requester: requester1 
Username of Supervisor: supervisor1  
Username of Manager:  manager1
Username of Admin   : admin
Password : 123456 >>for all user



>>How to Run the Application

1. Start the local development server using Artisan:
	php artisan serve
2. Open browser and navigate to [http://127.0.0.1:8000]. 



>>How to Run Automated Tests

php artisan test



 


